  "paragraph": 1,
  "text": "Put two AI coding agents powered by the identical frontier language model on the exact same engineering bug: fixing a token refresh race condition in an authentication module. On real benchmarks like SWE-bench and Terminal-Bench, and across tools like Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Devin, and OpenHands, you see the same striking paradox. One agent burns twenty turns in a broken retry loop and fails. The other isolates the bug, patches cleanly, and passes every test. Same weights, same intelligence, completely different outcome.",
